  "notes": "West leads the ♥J against 7NT. West's heart opening lead goes to the ♥A. South starts by cashing 2 top clubs. Luckily East's singleton club is the ♣10.\n\nThere will be no problem if diamonds run. West cannot hold a diamond guard because that would leave East with 5 spades. He would not have opened with a weak 2 bid in hearts.\n\nIf East has a diamond stopper, a simple squeeze in hearts diamonds will not function as the ♠A cannot be cashed before the long clubs. However, South can succeed on a repeating squeeze if East also has the ♠K. South should finish the clubs discarding the ♠A from the dummy.\n\nOn the last club a diamond discard from East will immediately give up 2 tricks. A spade or heart discard will set up a winner for South. Cashing that winner will subject East to a second squeeze.",
